[Event "01. The king is a fighting piece (1/4)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "5k2/8/8/8/3P4/K7/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "01. The king is a fighting piece (1/4)"]
[LineDescription "A far-away king walks to the centre first: from there it gets in front of its pawn."]

{[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6] [%cal Rd4d5] Welcome to Endgame Basics! First principle: in
the endgame the king is a fighting piece. With so few pieces left it is safe, so
bring it to the centre and in front of your pawn. Your king is far away: march
it to the centre first. Pushing the pawn now would only draw. Green: the key
squares (with your king on one, the pawn will queen). Red arrow: the push that
would only draw.} 1. Kb4 {The king heads for the centre. (d5 would only draw.)}
1... Ke7 {[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6]} 2. Kc5 Ke6 {[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6]} 3. Kc6 {Key square
c6! With your king here the pawn will queen whatever Black does.} 3... Ke7
{[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6]} 4. d5 {Now the pawn advances, escorted by the king.} 4...
Kd8 {[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]} 5. Kd6 {Opposition: the kings face each
other, and Black has to give way.} 5... Kc8 {[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]} 6.
Ke7 {The king walks ahead of the pawn and clears the way.} 6... Kc7 {[%csl
Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]} 7. d6+ {Pawn forward, with check.} 7... Kc6 {[%csl
Gc7,Gd7,Ge7,Gc8,Gd8,Ge8]} 8. d7 {The pawn reaches the 7th rank, and your king
guards the queening square.} 8... Kc7 {[%csl Gd8]} 9. d8=Q+ {Queen! The pawn has
promoted safely, and king and queen against king is a win (lesson 3).} *

[Event "01. The king is a fighting piece (2/4)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "1k6/8/8/8/5P2/8/2K5/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "01. The king is a fighting piece (2/4)"]
[LineDescription "A far-away king walks to the centre first: from there it gets in front of its pawn."]

{[%csl Ge6,Gf6,Gg6] [%cal Rf4f5] Far away again: centralise the king first, the
pawn can wait.} 1. Kd3 {The king heads for the centre. (f5 would only draw.)}
1... Kc7 {[%csl Ge6,Gf6,Gg6]} 2. Ke4 Kd6 {[%csl Ge6,Gf6,Gg6]} 3. Kf5 Ke7 {[%csl
Ge6,Gf6,Gg6]} 4. Kg6 {Key square g6! With your king here the pawn will queen
whatever Black does.} 4... Kf8 {[%csl Ge6,Gf6,Gg6]} 5. Kf6 {[%also f5]
Opposition: the kings face each other, and Black has to give way.} 5... Ke8
{[%csl Ge6,Gf6,Gg6]} 6. Kg7 {The king walks ahead of the pawn and clears the
way.} 6... Kd7 {[%csl Ge6,Gf6,Gg6]} 7. f5 {Now the pawn advances, escorted by
the king.} 7... Ke7 {[%csl Ge6,Gf6,Gg6,Ge7,Gf7,Gg7]} 8. f6+ {Pawn forward, with
check.} 8... Ke6 {[%csl Ge7,Gf7,Gg7,Ge8,Gf8,Gg8]} 9. f7 {The pawn reaches the
7th rank, and your king guards the queening square.} 9... Ke7 {[%csl Gf8]} 10.
f8=Q+ {Queen! The pawn has promoted safely, and king and queen against king is a
win (lesson 3).} *

[Event "01. The king is a fighting piece (3/4)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
