[LineName "01. The king is a fighting piece (3/4)"]
[LineDescription "The king leads and the pawn follows: the king clears the way to the queening square."]

{[%csl Gd6,Ge6,Gf6] [%cal Re4e5] The king stands next to its pawn. Pushing now
would only draw: the king goes first and clears the way.} 1. Kd5 {The king heads
for the centre. (e5 would only draw.)} 1... Kf6 {[%csl Gd6,Ge6,Gf6]} 2. Kd6 {Key
square d6! With your king here the pawn will queen whatever Black does.} 2...
Kf7 {[%csl Gd6,Ge6,Gf6]} 3. e5 {Now the pawn advances, escorted by the king.}
3... Ke8 {[%csl Gd6,Ge6,Gf6,Gd7,Ge7,Gf7]} 4. Ke6 {Opposition: the kings face
each other, and Black has to give way.} 4... Kd8 {[%csl
Gd6,Ge6,Gf6,Gd7,Ge7,Gf7]} 5. Kf7 {The king walks ahead of the pawn and clears
the way.} 5... Kd7 {[%csl Gd6,Ge6,Gf6,Gd7,Ge7,Gf7]} 6. e6+ {Pawn forward, with
check.} 6... Kd6 {[%csl Gd7,Ge7,Gf7,Gd8,Ge8,Gf8]} 7. e7 {The pawn reaches the
7th rank, and your king guards the queening square.} 7... Kd7 {[%csl Ge8]} 8.
e8=Q+ {Queen! The pawn has promoted safely, and king and queen against king is a
win (lesson 3).} *

[Event "01. The king is a fighting piece (4/4)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/8/8/8/6Pk/4K3/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "01. The king is a fighting piece (4/4)"]
[LineDescription "The king leads and the pawn follows: the king clears the way to the queening square."]

{[%csl Gf5,Gg5,Gh5] [%cal Rg3g4] King first, pawn later.} 1. Kf3 {The king heads
for the centre. (g4 would only draw.) Opposition: the kings face each other, and
Black has to give way.} 1... Kh2 {[%csl Gf5,Gg5,Gh5]} 2. g4 {Now the pawn
advances, escorted by the king.} 2... Kh3 {[%csl Gf6,Gg6,Gh6]} 3. g5 Kh4 {[%csl
Gf6,Gg6,Gh6,Gf7,Gg7,Gh7]} 4. g6 Kg5 {[%csl Gf7,Gg7,Gh7,Gf8,Gg8,Gh8]} 5. g7 Kf6
{[%csl Gg8]} 6. g8=Q {Queen! The pawn has promoted safely, and king and queen
against king is a win (lesson 3).} *

[Event "02. Mating patterns on the edge and in the corner (1/6)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "1k6/4Q3/2K5/8/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "02. Mating patterns on the edge and in the corner (1/6)"]
[LineDescription "Queen next to the king and protected by your king: checkmate."]

{[%csl Bc8,Ba8] First learn what the finish looks like. On the edge or in the
corner a king has only a few squares, so a queen or a rook can mate it with the
help of your king. Mate in 1 with the queen right next to the black king,
protected by your king. Blue: the squares the black king can step to. Find the
check that takes them all away.} 1. Qb7# {[%csl Rb8] Checkmate! The queen stands
right next to the black king, and your king protects it.} *

[Event "02. Mating patterns on the edge and in the corner (2/6)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "1k6/8/1K6/5Q2/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "02. Mating patterns on the edge and in the corner (2/6)"]
[LineDescription "Edge mate: your king takes the squares in front, the queen checks along the edge."]

{[%csl Ba8] Mate in 1. The kings face each other: your king covers the squares
in front of the black king, so the queen only has to check along the edge.} 1.
Qf8# {[%csl Rb8] Checkmate on the edge! The queen checks along the edge and your
king covers the squares in front.} *

[Event "02. Mating patterns on the edge and in the corner (3/6)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "1Q3K1k/8/8/8/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "02. Mating patterns on the edge and in the corner (3/6)"]
[LineDescription "In the corner the king has only three squares: your king covers two, the queen gives check."]

{[%csl Bh7] Mate in 1. In the corner the black king has only three squares: your
king takes two of them. Find the queen check that does the rest.} 1. Qh2# {[%csl
Rh8] Checkmate in the corner! The queen gives check and your king covers the
other squares.} *

[Event "02. Mating patterns on the edge and in the corner (4/6)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "2k5/4R3/2K5/8/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "02. Mating patterns on the edge and in the corner (4/6)"]
[LineDescription "Rook mate on the edge: kings face to face, rook check along the edge."]

{[%csl Bd8,Bb8] Mate in 1. The rook mates on the edge the same way: kings face
to face, rook check along the edge.} 1. Re8# {[%csl Rc8] Checkmate on the edge!
The rook checks along the edge and your king covers the squares in front.} *

[Event "02. Mating patterns on the edge and in the corner (5/6)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "7k/1R6/6K1/8/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "02. Mating patterns on the edge and in the corner (5/6)"]
[LineDescription "Corner mate: your king a knight's jump away, the rook checks along the edge."]

{[%csl Bg8] Mate in 1 in the corner: your king stands a knight's jump away and
covers the squares in front of the black king.} 1. Rb8# {[%csl Rh8] Checkmate in
the corner! The rook gives check and your king covers the other squares.} *

[Event "02. Mating patterns on the edge and in the corner (6/6)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "2k5/8/3K4/6R1/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "02. Mating patterns on the edge and in the corner (6/6)"]
[LineDescription "A waiting move forces the black king to step in front of yours: then the rook mates."]

{[%csl Bd8,Bb7,Bb8] Mate in 2. A rook check now would let the king escape. Make
a quiet waiting move with the rook: the black king has to step in front of
yours, and then the rook mates.} 1. Rb5 {A waiting move! The rook keeps the king
locked in, and now Black has to move: step in front of your king (and be mated)
or step back.} 1... Kd8 {[%csl Be8,Bc8]} 2. Rb8# {[%csl Rd8] Checkmate on the
edge! The rook checks along the edge and your king covers the squares in front.}
*

[Event "03. Checkmate with the queen (1/5)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "1Q5K/8/8/3k4/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "03. Checkmate with the queen (1/5)"]
[LineDescription "Queen a knight's jump from the black king: the box shrinks without a check."]

{[%csl
Bc1,Bd1,Be1,Bf1,Bg1,Bh1,Bc2,Bd2,Be2,Bf2,Bg2,Bc3,Bd3,Be3,Bf3,Bh3,Bc4,Bd4,Be4,Bg4,Bh4,Bc5,Bd5,Bf5,Bg5,Bh5,Bc6,Be6,Bf6,Bg6,Bh6,Bd7,Be7,Bf7]
King and queen against king always wins, in at most 10 moves. The plan: shrink
the black king's box with the queen, bring your king, mate on the edge. Every
move here is the fastest mate. The key move: put the queen a knight's jump away
from the black king. It takes away a whole block of squares without giving
check. Blue: the box, every square the black king can still reach. It shrinks
and never grows.} 1. Qb4 {The queen goes a knight's jump away from the black
king: the box shrinks to 16 squares.} 1... Ke5 {[%csl
Bd5,Be5,Bf5,Bg5,Bh5,Bc6,Be6,Bf6,Bg6,Bh6,Bc7,Bd7,Bf7,Bc8,Bd8,Be8]} 2. Kg7 {Your
king comes closer: the queen cannot mate on its own.} 2... Kd5 {[%csl
Bd5,Be5,Bf5,Bg5,Bh5,Bc6,Be6,Bc7,Bd7,Bc8,Bd8,Be8]} 3. Kf6 Kc6 {[%csl
Bd5,Bc6,Bc7,Bd7,Bc8,Bd8,Be8]} 4. Ke6 Kc7 {[%csl Bc6,Bc7,Bc8,Bd8,Be8]} 5. Qb5 {A
knight's jump again: 3 squares left.} 5... Kc8 {[%csl Bc7,Bc8,Bd8]} 6. Kd6 Kd8
{[%csl Bc8,Bd8]} 7. Qd7# {[%csl Rd8] [%also Qb8#] Checkmate! The queen stands
right next to the black king, and your king protects it.} *

[Event "03. Checkmate with the queen (2/5)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "1Q6/8/4k3/1K6/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "03. Checkmate with the queen (2/5)"]
[LineDescription "Queen a knight's jump from the black king: the box shrinks without a check."]

{[%csl
Ba1,Bb1,Bc1,Bd1,Be1,Bf1,Bg1,Bh1,Ba2,Bb2,Bc2,Bd2,Be2,Bf2,Bg2,Ba3,Bb3,Bc3,Bd3,Be3,Bf3,Bh3,Bd4,Be4,Bg4,Bh4,Bd5,Bf5,Bg5,Bh5,Be6,Bf6,Bg6,Bh6,Bd7,Be7,Bf7,Bg7,Bh7]
Find the queen move a knight's jump from the black king.} 1. Qf4 {The queen goes
a knight's jump away from the black king: the box shrinks to 10 squares.} 1...
Kd5 {[%csl Bd5,Be6,Ba7,Bb7,Bd7,Be7,Ba8,Bc8,Bd8,Be8]} 2. Kb6 {Your king comes
closer: the queen cannot mate on its own.} 2... Ke6 {[%csl
Bd5,Be6,Bd7,Be7,Bc8,Bd8,Be8]} 3. Kc6 Ke7 {[%csl Be6,Be7,Bc8,Bd8,Be8]} 4. Qf5 {A
knight's jump again: 3 squares left.} 4... Ke8 {[%csl Be7,Bd8,Be8]} 5. Kd6 Kd8
{[%csl Bd8,Be8]} 6. Qd7# {[%csl Rd8] [%also Qf8#] Checkmate! The queen stands
right next to the black king, and your king protects it.} *

[Event "03. Checkmate with the queen (3/5)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "1k6/3Q4/8/8/4K3/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "03. Checkmate with the queen (3/5)"]
[LineDescription "With the black king on the edge, the queen holds the box while your king comes to help."]

{[%csl Ba8,Bb8] The black king is already on the edge, but the queen cannot mate
on its own. Bring your king!} 1. Kd5 {Your king comes closer: the queen cannot
mate on its own.} 1... Ka8 {[%csl Ba8,Bb8]} 2. Kc6 Kb8 {[%csl Ba8,Bb8]} 3. Qb7#
{[%csl Rb8] Checkmate! The queen stands right next to the black king, and your
king protects it.} *

[Event "03. Checkmate with the queen (4/5)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "2Q5/8/3k4/8/8/2K5/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "03. Checkmate with the queen (4/5)"]
[LineDescription "Shrink the box, bring the king, mate on the edge."]

{[%csl
Ba1,Bb1,Bc1,Bd1,Be1,Bf1,Bg1,Bh1,Ba2,Be2,Bf2,Bg2,Bh2,Ba3,Be3,Bf3,Bg3,Ba4,Be4,Bf4,Bh4,Ba5,Bb5,Bd5,Be5,Bg5,Bh5,Bb6,Bd6,Bf6,Bg6,Bh6,Ba7,Be7,Bf7,Bg7,Bh7]
From the middle of the board: shrink the box with the queen, bring your king,
then mate.} 1. Kd4 {Your king comes closer: the queen cannot mate on its own.}
1... Ke7 {[%csl
Bd1,Be1,Bf1,Bg1,Bh1,Bd2,Be2,Bf2,Bg2,Bh2,Bf3,Bg3,Bf4,Bh4,Bg5,Bh5,Bd6,Bf6,Bg6,Bh6,Be7,Bf7,Bg7,Bh7]}
2. Ke5 Kf7 {[%csl
Bd1,Be1,Bf1,Bg1,Bh1,Bd2,Be2,Bf2,Bg2,Bh2,Bd3,Be3,Bf3,Bg3,Bh4,Bg5,Bh5,Bg6,Bh6,Be7,Bf7,Bg7,Bh7]}
3. Qg4 {[%also Kf5,Qh8] The queen takes more squares: the box shrinks to 16.}
3... Ke7 {[%csl
Ba5,Bb5,Bc5,Ba6,Bb6,Bc6,Ba7,Bb7,Bc7,Be7,Bf7,Ba8,Bb8,Bd8,Be8,Bf8]} 4. Qg7+
{Check! The black king has to step back: 6 squares left in its box.} 4... Kd8
{[%csl Ba8,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8,Be8]} 5. Kd6 Kc8 {[%csl Ba8,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8,Be8]} 6. Qc7#
{[%csl Rc8] Checkmate! The queen stands right next to the black king, and your
king protects it.} *

[Event "03. Checkmate with the queen (5/5)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "3Q4/8/4k3/8/7K/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "03. Checkmate with the queen (5/5)"]
[LineDescription "Shrink the box, bring the king, mate on the edge."]

{[%csl
Be1,Bf1,Bg1,Bh1,Be2,Bf2,Bg2,Bh2,Be3,Bf3,Be4,Bf4,Be5,Bf5,Be6,Bg6,Bh6,Bf7,Bg7,Bh7]
The whole plan again: box, king, mate.} 1. Qd4 {The queen goes a knight's jump
away from the black king: the box shrinks to 10 squares.} 1... Kf5 {[%csl
Bf5,Be6,Bg6,Bh6,Be7,Bf7,Bh7,Be8,Bf8,Bg8]} 2. Kh5 {Your king comes closer: the
queen cannot mate on its own.} 2... Ke6 {[%csl Bf5,Be6,Be7,Bf7,Bh7,Be8,Bf8,Bg8]}
3. Kg6 Ke7 {[%csl Be6,Be7,Be8,Bf8,Bg8]} 4. Qd5 {A knight's jump again: 3 squares
left.} 4... Ke8 {[%csl Be7,Be8,Bf8]} 5. Kf6 Kf8 {[%csl Be8,Bf8]} 6. Qf7# {[%csl
Rf8] [%also Qa8#,Qd8#] Checkmate! The queen stands right next to the black king,
and your king protects it.} *

[Event "04. Checkmate with the rook (1/5)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "1R6/8/3K4/5k2/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "04. Checkmate with the rook (1/5)"]
[LineDescription "The rook cuts the king off; with your king's help the box shrinks row by row."]

{[%csl
Bc1,Bd1,Be1,Bf1,Bg1,Bh1,Bc2,Bd2,Be2,Bf2,Bg2,Bh2,Bc3,Bd3,Be3,Bf3,Bg3,Bh3,Bc4,Bd4,Be4,Bf4,Bg4,Bh4,Bf5,Bg5,Bh5,Bf6,Bg6,Bh6,Bf7,Bg7,Bh7]
King and rook against king wins too, but takes longer. The plan: cut the king
off with the rook, bring your king, and check on the edge when the kings stand
face to face. Every move here is the fastest mate. The rook cuts the black king
off along a rank or a file. Each rook move then shrinks the box, while your king
comes closer and protects the rook. Blue: the box, every square the black king
can still reach. It never grows.} 1. Rb4 {The rook cuts the king off: the box
shrinks to 15 squares.} 1... Kf6 {[%csl
Bf5,Bg5,Bh5,Bf6,Bg6,Bh6,Bf7,Bg7,Bh7,Bc8,Bd8,Be8,Bf8,Bg8,Bh8]} 2. Rb5 {The box
shrinks to 12 squares.} 2... Kf7 {[%csl
Bf6,Bg6,Bh6,Bf7,Bg7,Bh7,Bc8,Bd8,Be8,Bf8,Bg8,Bh8]} 3. Rf5+ {Check! The black king
has to step back.} 3... Kg6 {[%csl Bg6,Bh6,Bg7,Bh7,Bg8,Bh8] Black attacks the
rook!} 4. Ke6 {Your king protects the rook and faces the black king.} 4... Kg7
{[%csl Bg6,Bh6,Bg7,Bh7,Bg8,Bh8]} 5. Rf6 {[%also Rg5+] The box shrinks to 4
squares.} 5... Kg8 {[%csl Bg7,Bh7,Bg8,Bh8]} 6. Rf7 {[%also Rg6+] The box shrinks
to 2 squares.} 6... Kh8 {[%csl Bg8,Bh8]} 7. Kf6 {[%also Kf5] Your king comes
closer: the rook cannot mate on its own.} 7... Kg8 {[%csl Bg8,Bh8]} 8. Kg6
{Opposition: the kings face each other with one square between them.} 8... Kh8
{[%csl Bg8,Bh8]} 9. Rf8# {[%csl Rh8] Checkmate in the corner! The rook gives
check and your king covers the other squares.} *

[Event "04. Checkmate with the rook (2/5)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/3k4/8/3K4/8/8/2R5 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "04. Checkmate with the rook (2/5)"]
[LineDescription "The rook cuts the king off; with your king's help the box shrinks row by row."]

{[%csl
Bd2,Be2,Bf2,Bg2,Bh2,Bf3,Bg3,Bh3,Bf4,Bg4,Bh4,Bf5,Bg5,Bh5,Bd6,Be6,Bf6,Bg6,Bh6,Bd7,Be7,Bf7,Bg7,Bh7,Bd8,Be8,Bf8,Bg8,Bh8]
Cut the king off and shrink the box.} 1. Re1 {The rook cuts the king off: the
box shrinks to 22 squares.} 1... Kc6 {[%csl
Ba2,Bb2,Bc2,Bd2,Ba3,Bb3,Ba4,Bb4,Ba5,Bb5,Ba6,Bb6,Bc6,Bd6,Ba7,Bb7,Bc7,Bd7,Ba8,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8]}
2. Re3 {[%also Re2,Kc4,Re6+,Re4] The box shrinks to 16 squares.} 2... Kd6 {[%csl
Ba4,Bb4,Ba5,Bb5,Ba6,Bb6,Bc6,Bd6,Ba7,Bb7,Bc7,Bd7,Ba8,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8]} 3. Kc4 {Your
king comes closer: the rook cannot mate on its own.} 3... Kc6 {[%csl
Ba4,Ba5,Ba6,Bb6,Bc6,Bd6,Ba7,Bb7,Bc7,Bd7,Ba8,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8]} 4. Rd3 {The box
shrinks to 11 squares.} 4... Kb6 {[%csl
Ba4,Ba5,Ba6,Bb6,Bc6,Ba7,Bb7,Bc7,Ba8,Bb8,Bc8]} 5. Rd6+ {Check! The black king has
to step back.} 5... Kb7 {[%csl Ba7,Bb7,Bc7,Ba8,Bb8,Bc8]} 6. Kb5 {Opposition: the
kings face each other with one square between them.} 6... Kc7 {[%csl
Ba7,Bb7,Bc7,Ba8,Bb8,Bc8] Black attacks the rook!} 7. Rd1 {[%also
Rd2,Rd3,Rd4,Rd5] The rook steps away from the black king without opening the
box.} 7... Kb7 {[%csl Ba7,Bb7,Bc7,Ba8,Bb8,Bc8]} 8. Rc1 {The box shrinks to 4
squares.} 8... Ka8 {[%csl Ba7,Bb7,Ba8,Bb8]} 9. Ka6 {[%also Kb6,Rc7] Opposition
again.} 9... Kb8 {[%csl Ba8,Bb8]} 10. Rc2 {[%also Rc3,Rc4,Rc5,Rc6,Kb6] A waiting
move! The rook keeps the king locked in, and now Black has to move: step in
front of your king (and be mated) or step back.} 10... Ka8 {[%csl Ba8,Bb8]} 11.
Rc8# {[%csl Ra8] Checkmate in the corner! The rook gives check and your king
covers the other squares.} *

[Event "04. Checkmate with the rook (3/5)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "3K4/6k1/5R2/8/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "04. Checkmate with the rook (3/5)"]
[LineDescription "When the kings face each other on the edge, a rook check is mate."]

{[%csl Bg7,Bh7,Bg8,Bh8] Bring your king in front of the black king: the
opposition. When Black has to move, his king must give way, or step in front of
yours and be mated.} 1. Ke7 {Your king protects the rook and faces the black
king.} 1... Kg8 {[%csl Bg7,Bh7,Bg8,Bh8]} 2. Rf7 {[%also Rg6+] The rook cuts the
king off: the box shrinks to 2 squares.} 2... Kh8 {[%csl Bg8,Bh8]} 3. Kf6 {Your
king comes closer: the rook cannot mate on its own.} 3... Kg8 {[%csl Bg8,Bh8]}
4. Kg6 {Opposition: the kings face each other with one square between them.}
4... Kh8 {[%csl Bg8,Bh8]} 5. Rf8# {[%csl Rh8] Checkmate in the corner! The rook
gives check and your king covers the other squares.} *

[Event "04. Checkmate with the rook (4/5)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "5R2/1k6/8/8/1K6/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "04. Checkmate with the rook (4/5)"]
[LineDescription "A waiting rook move: Black must step into the opposition (and is mated) or step back."]

{[%csl
Ba1,Bb1,Bc1,Bd1,Be1,Ba2,Bb2,Bc2,Bd2,Be2,Bd3,Be3,Bd4,Be4,Bd5,Be5,Ba6,Bb6,Bc6,Bd6,Be6,Ba7,Bb7,Bc7,Bd7,Be7]
Look out for the waiting move: when the kings are a knight's jump apart, the
rook slides along its rank and Black has to move.} 1. Kc5 {Your king comes
closer: the rook cannot mate on its own.} 1... Kc7 {[%csl
Ba1,Bb1,Bc1,Bd1,Be1,Ba2,Bb2,Bc2,Bd2,Be2,Ba3,Bb3,Bc3,Bd3,Be3,Ba4,Be4,Ba5,Be5,Ba6,Be6,Ba7,Bb7,Bc7,Bd7,Be7]}
2. Rf7+ {Check! The black king has to step back: 6 squares left in its box.}
2... Kd8 {[%csl Ba8,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8,Be8]} 3. Kd6 {Opposition: the kings face each
other with one square between them.} 3... Kc8 {[%csl Ba8,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8,Be8]} 4.
Re7 {[%also Rg7,Rh7] A waiting move! The rook keeps the king locked in, and now
Black has to move: step in front of your king (and be mated) or step back.} 4...
Kb8 {[%csl Ba8,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8]} 5. Kc6 Ka8 {[%csl Ba8,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8]} 6. Kb6 Kb8
{[%csl Ba8,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8]} 7. Re8# {[%csl Rb8] Checkmate on the edge! The rook
checks along the edge and your king covers the squares in front.} *

[Event "04. Checkmate with the rook (5/5)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "3R4/8/8/2k5/8/8/5K2/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "04. Checkmate with the rook (5/5)"]
[LineDescription "Cut off, bring the king, take the opposition, check on the edge: mate."]

{[%csl
Ba1,Bb1,Bc1,Ba2,Bb2,Bc2,Ba3,Bb3,Bc3,Ba4,Bb4,Bc4,Ba5,Bb5,Bc5,Ba6,Bb6,Bc6,Ba7,Bb7,Bc7]
The whole method from the middle of the board: cut off, bring the king, take the
opposition, check on the edge.} 1. Ke3 {Your king comes closer: the rook cannot
mate on its own.} 1... Kc4 {[%csl
Ba1,Bb1,Bc1,Ba2,Bb2,Bc2,Ba3,Bb3,Bc3,Ba4,Bb4,Bc4,Ba5,Bb5,Bc5,Ba6,Bb6,Bc6,Ba7,Bb7,Bc7]}
2. Rd4+ {Check! The black king has to step back.} 2... Kc5 {[%csl
Ba5,Bb5,Bc5,Ba6,Bb6,Bc6,Ba7,Bb7,Bc7,Ba8,Bb8,Bc8]} 3. Kd3 Kb5 {[%csl
Ba5,Bb5,Bc5,Ba6,Bb6,Bc6,Ba7,Bb7,Bc7,Ba8,Bb8,Bc8]} 4. Rc4 {The rook cuts the king
off: the box shrinks to 8 squares.} 4... Kb6 {[%csl
Ba5,Bb5,Ba6,Bb6,Ba7,Bb7,Ba8,Bb8]} 5. Kc3 Kb7 {[%csl
Ba5,Bb5,Ba6,Bb6,Ba7,Bb7,Ba8,Bb8]} 6. Kb4 {[%also Kb3]} 6... Kb6 {[%csl
Ba6,Bb6,Ba7,Bb7,Ba8,Bb8]} 7. Ka4 {[%also Rc1,Rc2,Rc3,Rc5]} 7... Ka7 {[%csl
Ba6,Bb6,Ba7,Bb7,Ba8,Bb8]} 8. Ka5 {[%also Kb5] Opposition: the kings face each
other with one square between them.} 8... Kb7 {[%csl Ba7,Bb7,Ba8,Bb8]} 9. Kb5
{Opposition again.} 9... Ka8 {[%csl Ba7,Bb7,Ba8,Bb8]} 10. Ka6 {[%also Kb6,Rc7]}
10... Kb8 {[%csl Ba8,Bb8]} 11. Rc1 {[%also Rc2,Rc3,Rc5,Rc6,Kb6] A waiting move!
The rook keeps the king locked in, and now Black has to move: step in front of
your king (and be mated) or step back.} 11... Ka8 {[%csl Ba8,Bb8]} 12. Rc8#
{[%csl Ra8] Checkmate in the corner! The rook gives check and your king covers
the other squares.} *

[Event "05. Don't stalemate! (1/5)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "2k5/4K3/8/8/8/8/8/1Q6 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "05. Don't stalemate! (1/5)"]
[LineDescription "When the black king has few squares left, make sure it still has one after your move (unless it is mate)."]

{[%csl Bc7] [%cal Rb1b6] Stalemate: the side to move is not in check but has no
legal move, and the game is a draw. It throws away many won endings, usually on
the last moves. Count the black king's squares before every move! The
knight's-jump trick can backfire: with the black king near the corner it may
leave no square at all. Blue: the squares the black king can step to. Red arrow:
the natural move that would be stalemate.} 1. Kd6 {Not Qb6: that would be
stalemate! Your king comes closer: the queen cannot mate on its own.} 1... Kd8
{[%csl Be8,Bc8]} 2. Qb8# {Checkmate on the edge! The queen checks along the edge
and your king covers the squares in front.} *

[Event "05. Don't stalemate! (2/5)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "7k/Q3K3/8/8/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "05. Don't stalemate! (2/5)"]
[LineDescription "Even a king move can stalemate: count the black king's squares first."]

{[%csl Bh7,Bg7,Bg8] [%cal Re7f8] Bringing your king closer can stalemate too.}
1. Kf6 {Not Kf8: that would be stalemate! Your king comes closer: the queen
cannot mate on its own.} 1... Kg8 {[%csl Bh8,Bf8]} 2. Qg7# {Checkmate! The queen
stands right next to the black king, and your king protects it.} *

[Event "05. Don't stalemate! (3/5)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "7k/1R6/5K2/8/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "05. Don't stalemate! (3/5)"]
[LineDescription "Before every move with the rook or the king, count the black king's squares."]

{[%csl Bg8] [%cal Rb7g7] The rook can stalemate as well.} 1. Kg6 {Not Rg7: that
would be stalemate! Your king comes closer: the rook cannot mate on its own.}
1... Kg8 {[%csl Bh8,Bf8]} 2. Rb8# {Checkmate on the edge! The rook checks along
the edge and your king covers the squares in front.} *

[Event "05. Don't stalemate! (4/5)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/5P1k/5K2/8/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "05. Don't stalemate! (4/5)"]
[LineDescription "When a new queen would stalemate, promote to a rook: it still wins."]

{[%csl Bh8,Bh6] Which piece should the pawn become? Count the black king's
squares first.} 1. f8=R {Rook! A queen on f8 would cover every square the black
king can go to: stalemate. The rook leaves it h6, and king and rook against king
is a win (lesson 4).} *

[Event "05. Don't stalemate! (5/5)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "5K1k/8/8/6P1/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "05. Don't stalemate! (5/5)"]
[LineDescription "A pawn push that leaves Black without a move is stalemate: move the king first."]

{[%csl Bh7] [%cal Rg5g6] The pawn push looks natural, but count Black's moves
first!} 1. Kf7 {g6 would be stalemate: the black king would have no move. The
king goes first. Key square f7! With your king here the pawn will queen whatever
Black does.} 1... Kh7 {[%csl Bh8]} 2. g6+ {Now the pawn advances, escorted by
the king.} 2... Kh6 {[%csl Bh5,Bg5]} 3. g7 {The pawn reaches the 7th rank, and
your king guards the queening square.} 3... Kh7 {[%csl Bh6]} 4. g8=Q+ {Queen!
The pawn has promoted safely, and king and queen against king is a win (lesson
3).} *

[Event "06. Final exam (1/6)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/1k6/8/3K4/2P5/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "06. Final exam (1/6)"]
[LineDescription "Active king, key squares, opposition: the pawn queens."]

{Final exam! No coloured squares this time. Use it all: an active king, the box,
the opposition, and no stalemate. Then try Practice mode without hints. King and
pawn: win it.} 1. Kd5 Kc7 2. Kc5 Kb7 3. Kd6 Ka6 4. c4 Kb7 5. c5 Kc8 6. Kc6 Kb8
7. Kd7 Kb7 8. c6+ Kb6 9. c7 Kb7 10. c8=Q+ {Queen! The pawn has promoted safely,
and king and queen against king is a win (lesson 3).} *

[Event "06. Final exam (2/6)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/8/6k1/8/4K3/5P2/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "06. Final exam (2/6)"]
[LineDescription "Active king, key squares, opposition: the pawn queens."]

{Another pawn ending.} 1. Ke4 Kf6 2. Kf4 Ke6 3. Kg5 Kf7 4. Kf5 Ke7 5. Kg6 Kd6 6.
f4 Ke7 7. f5 Kf8 8. Kf6 Ke8 9. Kg7 Ke7 10. f6+ Ke6 11. f7 Ke7 12. f8=Q+ {Queen!
The pawn has promoted safely, and king and queen against king is a win (lesson
3).} *

[Event "06. Final exam (3/6)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/2k5/8/3Q4/8/8/7K w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "06. Final exam (3/6)"]
[LineDescription "Box, king, mate: the queen mate."]

{King and queen: mate as fast as you can.} 1. Kg2 Kb5 2. Kf3 Kc6 3. Ke4 Kc7 4.
Qc5+ {[%also Kd5]} 4... Kb7 5. Kd5 Ka6 6. Qb4 Ka7 7. Kc6 Ka6 8. Qa3# {[%also
Qa4#,Qb6#] Checkmate on the edge! The queen checks along the edge and your king
covers the squares in front.} *

[Event "06. Final exam (4/6)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "1K6/6Q1/8/5k2/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "06. Final exam (4/6)"]
[LineDescription "Box, king, mate: the queen mate."]

{King and queen again.} 1. Qd4 Kg5 2. Qf2 {[%also Kc7,Kc8]} 2... Kg4 3. Kc7 Kg5
4. Kd6 Kg4 5. Ke5 Kg5 6. Qg3+ {[%also Qg2+,Qg1+]} 6... Kh5 7. Kf5 {[%also Kf6]}
7... Kh6 8. Qg6# {Checkmate! The queen stands right next to the black king, and
your king protects it.} *

[Event "06. Final exam (5/6)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "4R3/8/4K3/8/8/2k5/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "06. Final exam (5/6)"]
[LineDescription "Cut off, opposition, check on the edge: the rook mate."]

{King and rook: mate as fast as you can.} 1. Kd5 Kd3 2. Kc5 Kc3 3. Rd8 Kb3 4.
Rd3+ Kb2 5. Kb4 Kc2 6. Rd4 {[%also Rd5,Rd6,Rd7,Rd8]} 6... Kb2 7. Rc4 Ka1 8. Ka3
{[%also Kb3,Rc2]} 8... Kb1 9. Rc3 {[%also Rc5,Rc6,Rc7,Rc8,Kb3]} 9... Ka1 10.
Rc1# {Checkmate in the corner! The rook gives check and your king covers the
other squares.} *

[Event "06. Final exam (6/6)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
